WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:08.600
People are talking a lot about artificial intelligence (AI), viewing it as a force that could reshape how society works.
人们正在热议人工智能（AI），把它看作一股可能重塑社会运行方式的力量。

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.460
But there is something important missing from this discussion.
但这场讨论缺少了一样重要的东西。

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:15.570
It isn’t enough to ask how it will change us.
只问人工智能将如何改变我们，是不够的。

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:21.290
We also need to understand how we shape AI and what it can tell us about ourselves.
我们还需要了解自己是如何塑造人工智能的，以及它能告诉我们关于自身的哪些东西。

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:26.630
Every AI model we develop mirrors our rules and expresses our beliefs.
我们开发的每一个人工智能模型，都映照出我们的规则，表达着我们的信念。

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:36.240
A few years ago, while looking for new workers, a famous company gave up an AI-powered tool after finding it unfavorable to women.
几年前，一家著名公司在寻找新员工时，发现一款人工智能驱动的工具对女性不利，便放弃了这款工具。

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:43.670
The AI was not designed to behave this way; instead, it was influenced by the historical data favoring men.
这款人工智能并不是被设计成这样做的，而是受到了偏向男性的历史数据的影响。

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:54.970
Similarly, a recent study found that lending algorithms often offer less favorable terms to people of color, worsening long-standing unfairness in the money-lending business.
同样，最近的一项研究发现，贷款算法给有色人种提供的条件往往没那么优惠，加剧了放贷行业长期存在的不公平现象。

00:00:55.770 --> 00:01:02.060
In both cases, AI isn’t creating new biases; it is mirroring the ones that are already present.
在这两个例子中，人工智能都不是在制造新的偏见，而是在反映已经存在的偏见。

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:07.310
These reflections give us an important chance to take a close look at ourselves.
人工智能对偏见的这些反映，给了我们一个重要的机会，让我们仔细审视自己。

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:15.890
By making these problems visible and more pressing, AI challenges us to recognize and address what causes algorithmic bias.
人工智能让这些问题显现出来、变得更加紧迫，以此促使我们认清造成算法偏见的原因，并加以解决。

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:23.800
As AI continues to develop, we must ask ourselves how we as average people want to shape its role in society.
随着人工智能不断发展，我们必须问问自己：作为普通人，我们希望如何塑造它在社会中的角色。

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:31.020
We should not only improve AI models, but also make sure that AI is developed and used responsibly.
我们不仅应该改进人工智能模型，还应该确保以负责任的方式开发和使用人工智能。

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:34.440
A number of companies are already taking action.
一些公司已经在采取行动了。

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:40.000
They are judging the data, rules, and beliefs that shape the behavior of AI models.
它们正在评估那些塑造人工智能模型行为的数据、规则和信念。

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.900
Still, we cannot expect the companies to do all the work.
不过，我们不能指望这些公司包揽所有工作。

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:49.190
As long as AI is trained on human data, it will reflect human behavior.
只要人工智能是用人类的数据训练的，它就会反映人类的行为。

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:54.880
That means we have to think carefully about the footprints of ourselves we leave in the world.
这意味着，我们必须认真思考自己在世界上留下的足迹。

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:05.590
I may value privacy, but if I give it up in a heartbeat to visit a website, the algorithms may make a very different judgment of what I really want and what is good for me.
我或许看重隐私，但如果我为了访问一个网站就毫不犹豫地放弃隐私，那么对于我真正想要什么、什么对我有好处，算法作出的判断可能就会大不相同。

00:02:06.390 --> 00:02:18.650
If I want meaningful human connections yet spend more time on social media and less time in the physical company of my friends, I am indirectly training AI models about the true nature of humanity.
如果我想要有意义的人际联系，却在社交媒体上花更多时间，与朋友面对面相处的时间更少，那么我就是在间接地训练人工智能模型去认识人性的真实本质。

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:28.750
As AI becomes more powerful, we need to take increasing care to read our principles into the record of our actions rather than allowing the two to diverge.
随着人工智能变得更加强大，我们需要越来越用心，让我们的原则体现在自己的行为记录中，而不是任由两者脱节。

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:37.660
Recognizing this allows us to make better decisions, but only when we are prepared to look closely and take responsibility for what we see.
认识到这一点，能让我们作出更好的决定，但前提是我们愿意仔细审视，并对自己看到的东西负起责任。
